A||N||3||SilverFieroV6||auto tranny to 5 speed||||1||
Z||000000||SilverFieroV6||09-21-2000||10:34 PM||||what would you have to do to change a auto tranny to a 5spd on a fiero.  i am wondering cuz i want to change mine to a 5sp and i found a used camaro 2.8v6 with a new tranny in if for sale cheap.  second will that tranny fit in the fiero.  <BR>thanks for the info<BR>Sam CLark||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||09-21-2000||10:40 PM||||A tranny out of a Camaro will not fit in a Fiero.  The Camaro is rear wheel drive and uses a conventional tranny with a driveshaft to a rear axle.  You need the tranny out of a front wheel drive car.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||4
Z||000002||StuGood||09-22-2000||12:31 AM||||I bet a tranny from a Camaro <B>will</B> fit in a Fiero.  Be sure to put down something to protect the upholstery, though, or it'll probably get gear lube all over it.<P>Oooo, that smell - !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">    ||||reg||12
Z||000003||theogre||09-22-2000||10:00 AM||||Changing from auto to stick or the other way requires more than the tranny. You need to make a number of changes to the wiring and you need the right PROM for the ECM. That's in addition to bracketing and all the work to install the clutch hardware and plumbing.||||reg||1
